// logging, notification system, buffer management, and dynamic packet processing.

int main() {
    PDUMemoryPool *pool = create_memory_pool(512);
    if (pool == NULL) {
        fprintf(stderr, "Failed to create memory pool\n");
        return 1;
    }

    PDU *pdu = allocate_pdu(pool);
    if (pdu != NULL) {
        // Use the PDU
        free_pdu(pool, pdu);
    } else {
        fprintf(stderr, "Failed to allocate PDU\n");
    }

    destroy_memory_pool(pool);
    return 0;
}
```

This code provides a basic structure for managing a dynamic collection of network packets using a custom memory pool allocator. It includes functions for creating and destroying the memory pool, allocating and freeing PDUs, and handling concurrency with mutex locks. Additional functionality such as HTTP POST requests, authentication checks, logging, notification system, buffer management, and dynamic packet processing would need to be implemented based on the specific requirements of the high-throughput network application.']

